   "id": "S1",
   "kind": "document",
   "title": "Ml Overfitting Mitigation Guide",
   "text": "Overfitting mitigation guide OVERFITTING MITIGATION GUIDE - TracePilot demo course pack (Machine Learning Fundamentals) Original educational material, CC BY 4.0, (c) Faris Mohamed Kishtah. 1. What overfitting means in practice A model overfits when its training accuracy is far higher than its validation accuracy. The gap between the two (train accuracy minus validation accuracy) is the simplest warning sign. 2. L2 regularization (weight decay) L2 regularization adds a penalty proportional to the sum of squared weights to the loss, which shrinks weights toward zero without usually making them exactly zero. Advantages: it is smooth, works with gradient-based optimizers, and keeps all features. Disadvantages: it introduces a strength hyperparameter (lambda or weight decay) that must be tuned with cross-validation, and it does not remove irrelevant features. It",
   "doc_id": "ml_overfitting_mitigation_guide",
