  "S8": {
   "id": "S8",
   "kind": "document",
   "title": "Ml Model Diagnostics Handbook",
   "text": "1. Reading Learning Curves\nA learning curve plots training error and validation error against the training set size. In a high-bias\nmodel both errors are high and they converge close to each other; adding more data barely helps\nbecause the model is too simple. In a high-variance model the training error is low and a large gap\nseparates it from the validation error; the validation error keeps falling as more data is added, so\ncollecting more data helps.\nWhen a model is overfitting the first actions to try are a simpler model, stronger regularization,\nmore training data or early stopping.",
